t_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:b1566ff6a6e37da9719c7dd7e82cc9efb8dd1d8e963a9616986775fd42dcf5b9","file":"preprints/Beyond-the-Square-Root-Exponent-for-Depth-Three-Boolean-Circuits-September-23-2026/build/latex/sections/00_introduction.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"51e284d3c148555bca4db8fd310d9f63eb6387f3d939d446f251c28440139cf1","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Beyond-the-Square-Root-Exponent-for-Depth-Three-Boolean-Circuits-September-23-2026/build/latex/sections/00_introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:b1566ff6a6e37da9719c7dd7e82cc9efb8dd1d8e963a9616986775fd42dcf5b9","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Beyond-the-Square-Root-Exponent-for-Depth-Three-Boolean-Circuits-September-23-2026/build/latex/sections/00_introduction.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a language \\(L\\subseteq\\bits^*\\), a deterministic Turing machine\ndeciding \\(L\\), and fixed positive integers \\(C,a\\) such that the machine\nruns in time at most \\(C(n+1)^a\\) on every input of length \\(n\\).\nIf \\(f_n\\) is the membership function of \\(L\\) on \\(\\bits^n\\), then\n\\[\n \\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\log_2 S_3(f_n)}{\\sqrt n}=\\infty.\n\\]\nEquivalently, for every real \\(A>0\\), there is an integer \\(N_A\\)\nsuch that\n\\[\n S_3(f_n)>2^{A\\sqrt n}\\qquad\\text{for every }n\\ge N_A.\n\\]\nNo uniformity or bottom fan-in restriction is imposed on the circuits."}
